      "analytical_usefulness": 0.55,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Whether a goal states a numeric target is a meaningful practice dimension for achievement. However it is near-constant (548 Yes vs 2 No), giving little discriminating power for THIS query, capping usefulness. Values are well grounded: sampled descriptions all contain explicit percentages/counts."
    },
    {
      "name": "goal_duration_days",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Duration is a solid new axis to model against achievement. But values appear derived from start/end dates that are not clearly reflected in descriptions, and some are inconsistent with stated timeframes (e.g. a 'next quarter' goal at 316 days, a 'Q4' goal at 148, an 'upcoming year' at 477 vs a 20% cut labeled 11 days). Warranted where dates exist, but several look poorly grounded."
    },
    {
      "name": "priority_numeric",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.4,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A numeric recast of the existing 'priority' original column; trivially redundant, so it adds little analytical leverage beyond enabling sorting. Values are directly grounded in the priority field."
    },
    {
      "name": "achievement_vs_target",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.65,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A binned achievement measure is central to the query and a strong grouping axis. Derivable from percent_complete/target_percentage. However sample labels are inconsistent: the 78%->90% goal is 'Achieved' while a similar 75%->85% goal is 'Low Progress', and a 20% reduction is 'Achieved' with no visible completion evidence, indicating some ungrounded assignments."
    },
    {
      "name": "goal_outcome",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A consolidated outcome category is useful for outcome analysis, though it largely restates state + achievement_vs_target. Mostly derivable from state/percent_complete, but 'Cancelled' for the engagement-program row and other labels are not clearly supported by the sampled source text."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
  "source_groundedness": 0.68,
  "rationale": "Most columns provide genuine axes (specificity, quantified target, duration, achievement, outcome) directly relevant to what supports high achievement; priority_numeric and has_quantified_target are weaker due to redundancy and near-constancy respectively. Groundedness is moderate: quantified-target and priority values are well supported, but duration, achievement_vs_target, and goal_outcome show several assignments that conflict with or exceed the stated source text, indicating some fabricated specifics."
